    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:207-256`) applies. The method is guarded by `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`, so authorization is the first gate; then, in execution order:\n\n## Pre-validation short-circuit (idempotency)\n1. **Read `Idempotency-Key` header** (trimmed; blank \u2192 treated as absent). If present and an owner was already created under that key, **skip all validation and side-effects** and return that existing owner with `200 OK` (recomputing its `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag` for the response). Everything below runs only when this does not short-circuit.\n\n## Validations (each throws and aborts on failure)\n2. **Required fields** (`validateRequiredOwnerFields`): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (either structured `addressLine1` or flat `address`), `city`, `telephone` must be non-null/non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (collecting every missing field).\n3. **Registration date not in the future** (`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`): a supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`. (Absent date defaults to `LocalDate.now()`.)\n4. **Compute business day**: the supplied-or-defaulted date is rolled forward off weekends and the fixed public-holiday set (`toBusinessDay`) \u2192 this becomes the effective `registrationDate`.\n5. **Daily limit** (`rejectDailyLimitExceeded`): if \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100) existing owners already carry that business day \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException`.\n6. **City capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`): if the city (normalized) already holds \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) owners \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`.\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 Owner** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n8. **Postcode** (`validatePostcode`): optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region, within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`.\n9. **Telephone** (via `normalizeTelephone`, step 11): strips spaces/dashes/brackets, assumes `+61` when no `+` (dropping a leading `0`), must match `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and must have the exact national-number length for its country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`. (Validation and the side-effect of storing the E.164 value happen together.)\n10. **Email** (via `normalizeEmail`, step 14): optional; if present must match the email pattern and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`.\n11. **Duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`): if a non-deleted owner already has the identical `identityKey` (SHA-256 of normalized telephone + lower-cased email + Soundex of last name) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`.\n\n## Side-effects / mutations applied to the new owner\n12. **Address resolution** (`applyAddress`): normalizes address fields (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE); prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and composes `address`, else uses the flat `address` and clears the structured lines.\n13. **Telephone normalized & stored** (`setTelephone` with the E.164 value from step 9).\n14. **Household applied** (`applyHousehold`): if a postcode is present, derives and sets `householdId` (SHA-256 over version tag + normalized last name + postcode); returns whether the owner is a *declared* member of an existing household (existing member present **and** `sharesHousehold` true).\n15. **Email normalized & stored** (`setEmail` lower-cased, or null; from step 10).\n16. **Possible-duplicate flag** (`applyPossibleDuplicate`): a declared household member is never flagged; otherwise, if a non-deleted owner shares last-name Soundex + postcode but has a different identity key, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest-id match; else `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n17. **Registration date stored** (`setRegistrationDate` = the business day from step 4).\n18. **Member ID generated** (`generateMemberId`): `<REGION>V2<FY><HASH8><Luhn check digit>`, de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` on collision.\n19. **Namesake count stored** (`countNamesakes`): count of existing owners sharing normalized first + last name.\n20. **Idempotency key stored** (`setIdempotencyKey`, from step 1).\n21. **Membership-level ceiling** (`applyMembershipLevelCeiling`): if in a household, caps membership level at (max level among non-deleted household members) + 1.\n\n## Persistence and post-save side-effects\n22. **Save** (`clinicService.saveOwner`).\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 human-readable `Owner created:` line on the `AUDIT` logger.\n24. **Structured `OWNER_CREATED` event** (`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`): JSON with an incrementing sequence number on the `AUDIT` logger.\n25. **Welcome notification enqueued** (`enqueueWelcomeNotification`): line on the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n## Response assembly\n26. Builds `OwnerDto` and sets three computed response flags \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning` (`> 80` owners today), `capacityWarning` (city holds 40\u201349), `riskFlag` (possible duplicate OR disposable-adjacent email OR city over soft capacity \u2265 40) \u2014 sets the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, and returns `201 CREATED`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the header comment on `applyMembershipLevelCeiling` and the constant Javadocs describe intent, but the code above reflects the actual current behavior (e.g., the daily-limit and bulk-signup logic both key off the business-day-adjusted date, and the membership ceiling is applied only when a `householdId` was assigned)."
